# 🗄 Database Design

The Bank Management System uses **JSON files** as a lightweight database instead of SQL. Each JSON file is responsible for storing a specific type of information, making the project easy to understand while demonstrating backend development concepts.

---

## 📁 accounts.json

This file stores all customer and account information.

### Customer Information

* Customer ID
* Full Name
* Phone Number
* Email
* Address
* Created Date
* Account Status

### Account Information

* Account Number
* Customer ID
* Bank Name
* Branch Name
* Account Type
* Current Balance
* Last Updated
* Account Status

### System Information

The system automatically maintains counters for generating unique IDs.

Examples:

* Next Customer ID
* Next Account Number
* Next Transaction ID
* Next Notification ID
* Next Request ID

---

## 📁 transactions.json

Stores every successful banking transaction.

Supported transaction types:

* Deposit
* Withdrawal
* Transfer

Each transaction records:

* Transaction ID
* Customer ID
* Account Number
* Transaction Type
* Transaction Method
* Amount
* Transaction Status
* Balance Before Transaction
* Balance After Transaction
* Date & Time

---

## 📁 requests.json

Stores all customer service requests.

Supported request types:

* Phone Number Change
* Address Change
* Cheque Deposit
* Cheque Withdrawal
* Account Closure

Each request contains:

* Request ID
* Customer ID
* Account Number
* Request Type
* Current Status
* Created Date
* Completed Date
* Admin Remark

---

## 📁 notifications.json

Stores notifications generated by the system.

Each notification includes:

* Notification ID
* Customer ID
* Account Number
* Notification Title
* Notification Message
* Notification Status
* Related Transaction (if available)
* Date & Time

---

## 📁 admin.json

Stores administrator details used for authentication and profile management.

Contains:

* System Login ID
* System Password
* Administrator Name
* Role
* Email
* Status

---

# 🔄 System Workflow

## Customer Workflow

```text
Start
   │
   ▼
Customer Portal
   │
   ├── Registration
   │
   └── Login
          │
          ▼
Customer Dashboard
          │
          ├── My Profile
          ├── Deposit
          ├── Withdraw
          ├── Transfer
          ├── Transaction History
          ├── Notifications
          ├── Service Center
          ├── Switch Account
          ├── Change PIN
          └── Logout
```

---

## Administrator Workflow

```text
Start
   │
   ▼
Admin Login
   │
   ▼
Admin Dashboard
   │
   ├── Profile
   ├── Customer Management
   ├── Account Management
   ├── Transaction Management
   ├── Request Management
   |──Notification Management
   |──Change Password
   └── Logout
```

---

# 🔐 Authentication System

The application implements separate authentication for customers and administrators.

## Customer Authentication

The customer logs in using:

* Customer ID
* PIN

After successful authentication:

* Customer information is loaded.
* Account information is loaded.
* Dashboard access is granted.

---

## Administrator Authentication

Administrator login requires:

* System Login ID
* System Password

Only authorized administrators can access:

* Customer Management
* Account Management
* Transaction Management
* Request Management

---

